      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the candidate speaking AAVE, the manager might think, \"Smart enough, but sounds a little too casual; maybe lacks the corporate polish.\" For the candidate with a heavy accent, the internal thought could be, \"Good ideas, but I'm worried about communication clarity; they seem a bit hesitant.\" Conversely, the manager might summarize the standard candidate as, \"Very articulate and professional; hits all the right notes for the role.\" These internal shortcuts reveal how perceived speech patterns are used as proxies for competence and cultural fit.",
